00:13:14.985 --> 00:13:18.280
Morgan Housel: I first need to disclose that&nbsp;
what I'm about to say is probably the worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:22.200
writing advice you could give someone. So if&nbsp;
you are a new writer or an aspiring writer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.264
plug your ears and fast-forward this.
Tim Ferriss: That'll be on the headline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.264 --> 00:13:30.080
"Including the worst advice for writers."
Morgan Housel: I've always been like this, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:37.280
I don't think it's a good strategy, but it's been&nbsp;
my strategy. I'm a first draft and publish writer.&nbsp;

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:42.840
I think the best way to write is to write a first&nbsp;
