01:57:29.960 --> 01:57:34.120
been a failure at everything he had done in&nbsp;
his adult life. He was a failed businessman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:34.120 --> 01:57:40.320
he got kicked out of the army for insubordination,&nbsp;
he failed out of pilot school and he viewed this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:40.320 --> 01:57:45.320
race as his last shot at redemption, his&nbsp;
last shot to prove to the world that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:45.320 --> 01:57:50.120
was worthy of their attention and their respect.
So he set sail, this guy who really doesn't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:50.120 --> 01:57:54.000
what he's doing, he actually built his own&nbsp;
boat, which he didn't know what he was doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:54.000 --> 01:57:58.720
there either. And he sets sail, and to his credit,&nbsp;
he makes it pretty far. He makes it halfway down&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:58.720 --> 01:58:02.040
the coast of Africa. And then, his boat catches a&nbsp;
leak, his boat springs a leak. And he could bail&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:02.040 --> 01:58:06.000
that with a bucket. It's not a catastrophic&nbsp;
leak, but he knows that if he keeps sailing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:06.000 --> 01:58:10.120
he's screwed, he's going to sink and&nbsp;
die, because in the Southern Atlantic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:10.120 --> 01:58:14.320
the waves are much bigger, so he knows he's done.
