the winner. He's actually going to win this race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:13.960 --> 01:59:18.320
or at least appear to win this race. And&nbsp;
he realizes that that's a catastrophe&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:18.320 --> 01:59:21.547
because he's going to get so much attention&nbsp;
that they're going to uncover his fraud.&nbsp;

01:59:21.547 --> 01:59:23.440
Tim Ferriss: They're going to scrutinize it.
Morgan Housel: They're going to scrutinize it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:23.440 --> 01:59:29.920
and he's done. So now, he's very mentally unstable&nbsp;
at this point, as anyone for six months at sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:29.920 --> 01:59:36.400
alone would be. He realizes the jig is up. And&nbsp;
I'll cut to the chase and get to the punchline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:36.400 --> 01:59:42.800
His body was never found. His boat was found,&nbsp;
but the only plausible accepted outcome is that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:42.800 --> 01:59:48.560
after he realized it was all up, he threw himself&nbsp;
into the ocean, took his own life. And to me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:48.560 --> 01:59:55.240
it's a very astounding story of someone who&nbsp;
was so obsessed with gaining the respect and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:55.240 --> 01:59:59.640
admiration of other people. All he wanted to do&nbsp;
was for other people to admire him. That's it.&nbsp;

01:59:59.640 --> 02:00:05.880
And he wanted that so badly that he was willing&nbsp;
to have the six month fraud to deceive everybody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:05.880 --> 02:00:10.840
and when it didn't work, he just decided that life&nbsp;
wasn't worth living. And that, to me, is just an&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:10.840 --> 02:00:17.240
astounding mental state, that someone would want&nbsp;
respect from strangers and the press that badly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:17.240 --> 02:00:23.160
that it's worth everything to them. It's just an&nbsp;
astounding story of the lifestyle that you choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:23.160 --> 02:00:29.400
to live and the goals that you tend to have. He&nbsp;
wanted this goal more than anyone else, and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:29.400 --> 02:00:34.000
he couldn't have it, he took his own life.
There's a quote from Nassim Taleb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

